00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:45.149
SpaceX received Federal Communications Commission, or FCC, approval to deploy up to 1 million

00:03:45.149 --> 00:03:51.609
star-mind satellites for Orbital AI data centers. The first satellite is required by November 25th,

00:03:51.609 --> 00:03:59.929
2033, and 100,000 are required by 2035. The satellites will fly between 500 and 1,000

00:03:59.929 --> 00:04:06.289
two kilometers, use optical inter-satellite links for primary communication, and fall back to K-band

00:04:06.289 --> 00:04:12.089
radio when those links fail. A completed debris mitigation plan must be filed before any units

00:04:12.089 --> 00:04:18.489
operate above 600 kilometers. The same approval sets hard milestones at 500,000 satellites

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:26.789
by 2038, and full completion by 2040, or the authorization lapses. SpaceX has already contracted

00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:32.749
singulas for solar cell production equipment tied to the constellation. The FCC denied petitions

00:04:32.749 --> 00:04:39.389
from Amazon Leo, Viassat, and the American Astronomical Society. The lower orbit range chosen

00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:45.489
by the FCC reduces some latency concerns compared with the original 2000 km upper limit in the

00:04:45.489 --> 00:04:50.949
application. Those dates and quantities sit alongside Tesla's own need for massive inference

00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:57.349
compute to train and run both FSD and Optimus at scale. Placing the compute in orbit changes

00:04:57.349 --> 00:05:02.929
the power and cooling equations that constrain ground-based clusters, yet it still requires reliable

00:05:02.929 --> 00:05:08.509
downlink capacity and regulatory clearance for the full constellation. The 1 million satellite

00:05:08.509 --> 00:05:15.569
ceiling and the 2033-2040 timeline, therefore become concrete variables in any model that

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:20.709
forecasts how quickly Tesla can expand its AI training throughput beyond terrestrial limits.

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:26.209
Optical links between satellites enable the cluster-style computing approach SpaceX has

00:05:26.209 --> 00:05:31.309
described, while the K-band fallback provides a safety net for command and telemetry.

00:05:31.869 --> 00:05:36.849
Manufacturing contracts already signed indicate the company is moving from regulatory filing

00:05:36.849 --> 00:05:41.629
to hardware production on a timeline that aligns with the first launch target Musk mentioned

00:05:41.629 --> 00:05:43.329
at the Baron Investment Conference.

00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:48.869
For Tesla, any orbital capacity that becomes available would sit outside the power and

00:05:48.869 --> 00:05:52.929
land constraints that currently shape cortex and dojo expansion plans.

00:05:53.609 --> 00:05:58.029
The constellation is designed to meet growing demand for artificial intelligence computing

00:05:58.349 --> 00:06:02.049
by processing large amounts of data in orbit for use on Earth.

